WEBVTT

00:04:59.763 --> 00:05:01.431
we could share it.

00:05:01.464 --> 00:05:02.999
And not only could we share it,

00:05:03.033 --> 00:05:05.735
we could find other people
who would applaud,

00:05:05.735 --> 00:05:07.938
who would follow us, who'd fan us.

00:05:07.971 --> 00:05:09.272
And suddenly, oh my gosh,

00:05:09.272 --> 00:05:13.810
like, we've got all this access
to mass information at scale.

00:05:13.844 --> 00:05:16.646
And you could do this for free.

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:18.181
You could do this for free.

00:05:18.215 --> 00:05:21.685
So suddenly we're getting hit
with all this information,

00:05:21.718 --> 00:05:24.487
and I don't think our species
was built to keep up with it.

00:05:24.487 --> 00:05:26.723
I talked to a guy
at the University of Maryland

00:05:26.756 --> 00:05:28.792
who's studied students
for the last decade,

00:05:28.825 --> 00:05:32.395
and he basically found that even
when you choose to read something,